<BaseLayout
  title="Alexander K Saeri | AI risk research"
  description="I direct the MIT AI Risk Initiative, building the evidence base that decision-makers need to manage the most important risks from AI."
>
  <section class="lead-block">
    <h1>AI risk research for decision-makers.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I direct the <strong>MIT AI Risk Initiative</strong>, building the evidence base that decision-makers need to manage the most important risks from AI.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="https://airisk.mit.edu" class="btn">Explore the AI Risk Initiative</a>
      <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-outline">Request a meeting</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Image
    src={heroPhoto}
    alt="Alexander K Saeri speaking at EAGxAustralasia 2025 in Melbourne"
    class="header-banner"
    widths={[600, 1000, 1600]}
    sizes="(max-width: 850px) 100vw, 800px"
    loading="eager"
  />

  <div class="section" id="about">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>I conduct and communicate research to help govern highly capable general-purpose AI. I direct the MIT AI Risk Initiative at MIT FutureTech, and hold positions at MIT FutureTech and The University of Queensland. I'm based in Melbourne.</p>
    <p>My methods background is in social psychology, applied behaviour science, implementation science, evidence synthesis, systems thinking, and survey research.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section" id="airi">
    <h2>MIT AI Risk Initiative</h2>
    <p>I direct the AI Risk Initiative at MIT FutureTech. We provide data and frameworks to help decision-makers across the AI ecosystem identify, prioritise, and manage the most important risks from AI. Our work asks:</p>

    <ul class="workstreams">
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">What are the risks from AI?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/risks">AI Risk Repository</a> (<a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15LeHcpeuZC9txkvcaMoh3sUhkMvdMMry69xxXL46DT0/copy">database</a> | <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patter.2026.101517">paper</a>)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">Which risks matter most?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/priorities">AI Risk Priorities</a> (<a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/priority-risk-visualizations/severity-and-concern">database</a> | <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.04490">paper</a>)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">Where is AI already causing harm?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/ai-incident-tracker">AI Incident Tracker</a> (<a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/ai-incident-tracker/incident-overview">database</a>)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">How are the world's largest companies responding?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/company-disclosures">AI Risk Disclosure Tracker</a> (<a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/company-disclosures-explorer">database</a> | <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2611.04278">paper</a>)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">What can reduce the risks?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/ai-risk-mitigations">AI Risk Mitigation Repository</a> (<a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/mitigations-explorer">database</a> | <a href="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/669550d38372f33552d2516e/6aed5f43fa93bb92482b925b_mitigations-repository-mit-airi-2026.pdf">paper</a>)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="workstream-q">How is AI being governed?</p>
        <p class="workstream-links"><a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/ai-governance">AI Governance Map</a> (<a href="https://airisk.mit.edu/governance/document-view">database</a>)</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section" id="ecosystem">
    <h2>Australia's AI safety ecosystem</h2>
    <p>Alongside AIRI, I help build Australia's AI safety ecosystem. I advise AI safety organisations in Australia and mentor researchers and fellows in the community. I co-founded the <a href="https://maish.au/">Melbourne AI Safety Hub</a> coworking space and convene the <a href="https://aisum.org/">AI Safety Unconference</a> (2023, 2025 and 2026). I designed and facilitated the inaugural <a href="https://aisafetyforum.au/">Australian AI Safety Forum</a> in 2024 and spoke at the 2026 Forum.</p>
  </div>

